console.log(Serving cached fallback profile infromation.");
}} fetchUserProfile(42);
3. Always Add .catch() to PromisesPrefer standard Promises over ?Never leave a  block alone. Always end your Promise chain with .Always put  at the end of your chain. This handles network errors cleanly.Unmasking the Mystery of the "this" KeywordThe  keyword is easily one of the most confusing parts of learning JavaScript. At its core,  is like a dynamic pronoun in a sentence. Say a smartphone hits the floor and breaks. Your brain knows "it" means the phone.In JavaScript, this works like a pronoun. Its meaning changes based on where and how you use it. Misunderstanding these changing rules is a major cause of silent, unpredictable website behavior.   To master , you need to look at the four different environments where it changes its identity:1.  A function inside an object is called a method.     Here, this points directly to the parent object. It’s how an object talks about its own properties.`` javascript 
